# STUDENT SLIDESHOW FORGE — Creación Digital I / II

The student-facing surface is a short image-led Reveal.js deck, visually
consistent with “How to Pass This Track.” It is not the lesson text, a research
ledger, or an instructor script. The fuller unit lesson and session prompt are
professor-side preparation material; internal provenance remains source-only.

## Media intake: collection → accepted pack → deck

Never read a raw Profield discovery index directly into a public page. The
correct route is:

```text
media-index.json (review inbox)
→ media-collection.py named collection (editorial snapshot)
→ instructor review / acceptance
→ MP5 YAML pack in docs/_data/media-packs/
→ student deck slots matched by media_slot_id
```

Use the unit manifests under
`/Users/ruvebal/src/profield/runs/media-prospector/<UNIT>/<RUN>/manifest.json`,
not the root index, as the asset source. The accepted I.1 snapshot is
`I.1/20260904T130000Z/manifest.json`: two reviewed Wikimedia Commons images,
both CC BY-SA 4.0. They seed the first I.1 analysis deck. All other unit decks
remain blocked until their own accepted manifest/collection arrives; never
invent a replacement image, URL, credit, licence, or alt text.

Each deck slide receives only public-safe media fields: title, public preview or
embed URL, alt text, credit line, licence display, and the single sentence that
states what students should notice. Profield run IDs, local paths, retrieval
traces, review notes, rights uncertainty, and scholarly provenance never render.

## Production rehydration

Background selection is collection-driven. For each unit, the rehydrator reads
the accepted assets belonging to that unit's reviewed media collection, sorts
them by upstream priority/rank, and assigns the selected asset to the slide's
`media_slot_id`. The slot names the teaching role; it does not itself fetch an
image. A slide with no media slot keeps the theme background.

### Explicit slide-image override

The deck author may force a particular accepted catalogue asset for a specific
slide. Use this when the teaching argument depends on one named image rather
than on whichever asset currently ranks first:

```json
{
  "media_selection": {
    "unit_id": "I.1",
    "collection": "designers",
    "strategy": "explicit-then-ranked"
  },
  "media_overrides": {
    "I.1.still.profield-1": "wikimedia:File:Fan SAAM-1935.8.20 1.jpg",
    "I.1.still.profield-2": "wikimedia:File:Miss Maquillage Digital Fashion Garment example.png"
  }
}
```

The key is the slide's `media_slot_id`; the value is the Profield `asset_id`.
The rehydrator must resolve the override inside the selected reviewed
collection, require `review_status: accepted`, a rank from 1–5, a usable
public image or video URL, rights evidence, and accessibility metadata. A
missing, rejected, unranked, or non-renderable override is never silently
published: report it and fall back to the normal accepted unit/rank selection
for that slot. Overrides take precedence only for their named slots; all
other slots remain collection- and rank-driven. Preserve the asset's canonical
source and licence metadata in the deck output.

Priority is marked upstream in the unit manifest (`review.priority`, `priority`,
or `rank`). Run `npm run media:rehydrate` before the production build. The
script scans accepted manifests under `runs/media-prospector/`, deduplicates by
asset ID, sorts by priority, preserves the deck's `media_slot_id` mapping, and
copies only public-safe fields into the deck JSON. The production deck has no
reload control and no dependency on Profield paths at runtime.

## Unit deck shape

**Binding parallel contract:** [`SESSION-RHYTHM-AND-DELIVERABLES.mdc`](./SESSION-RHYTHM-AND-DELIVERABLES.mdc).

Ordinary unit deck spine (order binding):

1. **Question / title**
2–n. **Masterclass** moves (one idea per slide; Profield or diagram) — I.0 may use more taxonomy slides
n. **`lab_opener`** (geometrical) — exercises are about to begin; they go into the **portfolio index**
n+1…n+2. **Exactly two Lab exercises** (`lab_exercise`, `portfolio_bound: true`) — concentrate the unit’s meaning into **two** portfolio-bound tasks; do **not** forge three or more Lab exercises per lesson
m. **`workshop_opener`** / **`workshop_work`** — **only from session 4** (≈½ D2 Transposition · ≈½ D3 final event). **Omit entirely** on first lessons (I.1 / I.2 / sessions 1–3).
z. **`outro`** (geometrical) — carry-forward

**Lab exercise count (binding):** **2** per ordinary unit lesson/deck. Fold adjacent micro-drills into those two (practice map + field position for I.1; do not keep Boundary / JPEG / Directory as three separate exercises).

One conceptual move, one heading, one sentence, one visual focus per Masterclass slide.

Use visual-forger for course-generated diagrams. Use media-embed-forger only
after the MP5 pack passes validation. A student deck may name UEM and the course
only; it must not name Profield, Ahmes, Athanor, DevIAC, UDIT, Web Atelier, or
the sibling runtime.

## 120-minute class rhythm

| Block | ≈ minutes | Name | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Analysis strip | 00–30 | Modelled analysis (sessions 1–2) or **2×15 min** student defences (from session 3) | D1 defence slideshow |
| Masterclass | 30–60 | Professor ideas + Profield images | conceptual notes |
| **Lab (Portfolio)** | 60–90 | **Exactly two** exercises + debates — **must enter portfolio** | portfolio traces |
| **Workshop** | — / 90–120 | **Absent** in first lessons. From **session 4**: ≈½ **D2 Transposition** · ≈½ **D3 final event** | D2–D3 progress only |

**First lessons (I.1 / I.2 · sessions 1–3):** **No Workshop slides.** Session ends after Lab. Do **not** invent “studio piece this week” or any side deliverable. **D1 Analysis** is the next graded stake and is defended in the Analysis strip (from session 3) — it **never** receives Workshop clock.

**Lab ≠ Workshop.** Lab leaves portfolio traces. Workshop (from s4) is Transposition + final event only — not “whatever deliverable is next,” and never D1.

### Background law

| Role | Background |
| --- | --- |
| `unit_cover` | Profield still (I.1 opening: astronaut EVA still unless a later override is reviewed) |
| Masterclass content | Accepted Profield media or course diagram |
| `analysis_model` · `lab_exercise` · `workshop_work` | **Profield image background** when a unit asset exists — not `none` / not flat diagram |
| `lab_opener` · `workshop_opener` · `outro` · `analysis_opener` | **Geometrical only** |
| Never | Invented images; geometrical BG replacing a required Masterclass media slot |
| Never | `organic-pixel-drift` / “circle dancing” (or any non-henon decorative SVG) as a slide background — transitions use **henon geometrical** only, and the forge caption **must** include the SVG content-hash UUID from the filename |
| Lab/Workshop content without an accepted asset | `background_kind: none` (solid stage) until Profield assigns a slot — do **not** steal Masterclass images onto slides 10–12 |

### Quote hierarchy (revised 2026-09-15 · ∥ CT slideshow forge)

Every substantive slide (`unit_cover`, `analysis_model`, masterclass, `lab_exercise`, `workshop_work`) carries a brief, specific `quote:` that sharpens the sentence:

1. **Prefer Ahmes** — `semantic-quote` against `extraction.db`, `evaluator_safe=yes`. Provenance in a switch-gated lesson comment. `content.json`: verbatim + `quote_origin: ahmes` + Chicago `citation` linking into `## References`.
2. **Else invent** in the voice of **The Tao of the Image** (DC) and propose into TTOD via `ttod-bridge` (section `images` or nearest; never hand-edit `ttod.yml`). `quote_origin: tao_invented`, `citation.label: (Tao of the Image)`, invents are studio aphorisms — never disguised as scholarly quotation.
3. **Semantic tags required** whenever `quote` is set (not student-rendered by default): `semantic_tags.themes`, `.cidoc` (e.g. `crm:E33_Linguistic_Object`), `.getty_aat`, `.dcterms`.
4. **AI-declaration filiation** — Rubén Vega Balbás, PhD (`ruvebal@crea-comm.net`) only; never `(ECSIT / UEM)`.

## Course delivery and assessment choreography

Official weights stay in the UEM guía. Studio choreography (TC ∥ DC):

| Evidence | Student task | DC fork |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **D1 — Analysis** | 15 min in-person defence; support = slideshow; **2 students/session from session 3** | Fashion image related to a **Madrid exhibition** piece (coordinated visit with Spanish-cohort students) |
| **D2 — Transposition** | Critical review / palimpsest / discursive circulation | Output **into an image** (series OK) |
| **D3 — Atrium** | Tech script + live performance/defence | Theme: **Communicate and inspire: What is fashion for you?** |
| **D4 — Portfolio index** | Index of Lab exercises + D1–D3 | Same |
| **D5 — Exam** | Test/questionnaire + **final self-review** of portfolio process | Same |

D1 intra-rubric: presentation **70%** · deliverable support **20%** · peer debate **10%**.

