No Profield-backed slide is published until `media_slot_id` resolves to an accepted MP5 record
or the slide is a course-generated diagram / geometrical structural slide with accessible text.

## Publish gate — track + lesson links (fail-closed)

When a unit deck ships (`docs/tracks/en/uem/2627-dc*/…/index.html` + `content.json`), **all** of the following must exist before claiming the unit forged:

1. **EN track table** — unit row includes `· [slideshow]({{ '/tracks/dci|dcii/<slug>/' | relative_url }})` beside the lesson link.
2. **ES track table** — same deck URL as `· [presentación](…)` (decks are EN-only until a Spanish pack exists).
3. **EN + ES lesson frontmatter** — `deck_url: /tracks/dci|dcii/<slug>/`
4. **EN + ES lesson cover** — **In-class deck** / **Presentación en clase** link to that permalink, plus How-to-Pass rhythm line.

Do **not** invent slideshow links for scaffold units that have no deck folder yet
(I.4–I.9, remaining CD II units until forged). I.1–I.3 decks are live.

## Local Ollama forge phase

The ontology lecture and student slideshow use the locally installed model:

```bash
OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3.8:27b
```

Use the Ollama HTTP API with an explicit timeout. The model may draft lecture
structure, slide sentences, ontology-card prompts, and media-slot requests; it
may not invent citations, licences, image URLs, provenance, or rights status.
The deterministic forge remains authoritative for official contents, timing,
publication safety, visual-readability rules, and MP5 acceptance. If the model
is unavailable, fail closed rather than silently substituting another model.
